WEBVTT

00:00:42.110 --> 00:00:46.910
Darkness is an existence that
eventually consumes everything.

00:00:47.350 --> 00:00:49.690
When light is lost in an instant,

00:00:50.130 --> 00:00:52.650
all colors are devoured by pitch black.

00:01:25.370 --> 00:01:27.600
This new-found darkness

00:01:28.960 --> 00:01:33.990
drains the color out of existence.

00:01:59.170 --> 00:02:03.500
Distractions day after day, it's always something

00:01:59.170 --> 00:02:03.500
Meutsuri Shiteru Hibi Are Kore

00:02:03.780 --> 00:02:07.640
and no one has even realized that

00:02:08.330 --> 00:02:12.660
I see the crimson trailing down your cold skin

00:02:08.330 --> 00:02:12.660
Awadatsu Hada wo Tsutai Ochiru CRIMSON

00:02:12.850 --> 00:02:16.850
Why do you want another punishment?

00:02:12.850 --> 00:02:16.850
Why do you want Atarashii Batsu wo

00:02:17.480 --> 00:02:21.600
The sweet fragrances that are drifting about

00:02:17.480 --> 00:02:21.600
Tadayou Amai Kaori wo Tada

00:02:22.090 --> 00:02:26.160
I just want to leave them be

00:02:22.090 --> 00:02:26.160
Asobasete Itai Dake Nano sa

00:02:26.660 --> 00:02:33.840
Someone hurry up and shoot me

00:02:26.660 --> 00:02:33.840
Dareka Boku wo Hayaku Uchinuite yo

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:38.990
Show me a gunshot strong enough to make a hole

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:38.990
Show me Kantsuushita Juusou Ana ga Aku Hodo

00:02:39.210 --> 00:02:43.460
I crush my thorny grip

00:02:39.210 --> 00:02:43.460
Toge Darake no GRIP Nigiritsubushite

00:02:43.820 --> 00:02:49.230
and load bullets that look like ripe flowerbuds

00:02:43.820 --> 00:02:49.230
Osanai Mada Tsubomi no You na Dangan de

00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:53.340
Let me shoot through the soul

00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:53.340
Let me, shot through the soul

00:02:54.080 --> 00:02:58.290
and dye it rose

00:02:54.080 --> 00:02:58.290
Bara-iro ni Somare

00:03:27.970 --> 00:03:30.540
You've always been like this.

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:32.110
You haven't changed at all!

00:03:32.110 --> 00:03:33.340
You don't understand anything!

00:03:38.970 --> 00:03:42.390
Did you think killing
someone would be enjoyable?

00:03:42.740 --> 00:03:47.020
Did you honestly believe the way you
brought this up would make me feel better?

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:49.350
I-I'm sorry!

00:03:50.120 --> 00:03:52.010
U-Um, Aki—

00:03:52.600 --> 00:03:54.200
Cut the crap!

00:03:55.560 --> 00:03:58.450
Just looking at you irritates me.

00:03:58.880 --> 00:03:59.960
I'm sorry!

00:03:59.960 --> 00:04:01.780
About that... I'm—

00:04:02.290 --> 00:04:03.220
I'm sorry!

00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:05.260
Wait—

00:04:06.630 --> 00:04:07.810
Keisuke!

00:04:10.490 --> 00:04:12.740
Man, there he goes.

00:04:13.500 --> 00:04:16.810
Whatever. He'll be back in a second.

00:04:41.490 --> 00:04:44.080
The influx of goods has
been pretty bad lately.

00:04:44.480 --> 00:04:46.760
This vial's all I have left right now.

00:04:48.290 --> 00:04:51.990
Don't try to give me any cut down shit.

00:04:54.010 --> 00:04:59.310
I know there's dealers with
fifty-percent mixtures.

00:04:59.310 --> 00:05:02.570
What Vischio's been dealing so far
is only around thirty-percent.

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:04.690
Anything above that doesn't exist.

00:05:05.260 --> 00:05:07.690
Word on the street is they're
going around the market still.

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:38.010
What the hell happened here?

00:05:46.770 --> 00:05:47.900
Keisuke?

00:05:47.900 --> 00:05:49.010
Keisuke!

00:05:49.480 --> 00:05:50.470
Keisuke?!

00:06:06.220 --> 00:06:07.380
What happened here?

00:06:09.060 --> 00:06:10.890
I-I don't have any more Line!

00:06:11.610 --> 00:06:12.750
P-Please don't kill me!

00:06:15.280 --> 00:06:16.010
Wait for me!

00:06:34.140 --> 00:06:36.600
Wasn't this part of the neutral zone?

00:06:38.370 --> 00:06:40.340
Who would do this?

00:07:13.080 --> 00:07:13.440
Yo.

00:07:17.150 --> 00:07:20.400
What the hell are you doin'
in a place like this?

00:07:21.580 --> 00:07:23.570
You're that guy from before?!

00:07:24.350 --> 00:07:27.200
So you remember me.

00:07:27.200 --> 00:07:28.290
I'm thrilled.

00:07:28.810 --> 00:07:32.290
But I'm different from what I was before!

00:07:33.580 --> 00:07:35.380
I'll fuckin' kill you!

00:07:40.290 --> 00:07:41.380
Take that!

00:07:45.940 --> 00:07:47.970
Scared yet?

00:07:48.450 --> 00:07:51.940
What happened to all that aggression, Lost?!

00:07:52.650 --> 00:07:54.520
Let me have my fun!

00:07:56.810 --> 00:07:58.700
Die already!

00:07:58.700 --> 00:08:00.150
Take that!

00:08:02.340 --> 00:08:03.320
You idiot!

00:08:06.800 --> 00:08:09.140
Is that all you can do, Lost?

00:08:15.650 --> 00:08:18.880
You used Line?!

00:08:20.280 --> 00:08:21.800
What're you going to do about it?

00:08:22.840 --> 00:08:24.930
You're the one who did that to the club—

00:08:25.180 --> 00:08:27.550
Shut the fuck up!

00:08:29.530 --> 00:08:30.520
You're too slow!

00:08:33.460 --> 00:08:36.980
Looking down on people
like this feels amazing!

00:08:38.240 --> 00:08:42.900
I used to think it was pointless
even thinking about it.

00:08:43.260 --> 00:08:47.070
Now that I have this incredible strength,

00:08:48.890 --> 00:08:51.600
the invincible Lost can't even fight back!

00:08:51.600 --> 00:08:55.300
I told you before, Igra is
completely different than Bl@ster!

00:09:00.910 --> 00:09:03.940
You're slow as a turtle now!

00:09:03.940 --> 00:09:05.600
It's like you're not even moving.

00:09:05.600 --> 00:09:09.560
Do you know what'll happen to
you if you keep using Line?!

00:09:11.020 --> 00:09:12.220
What'd you just say?

00:09:12.580 --> 00:09:14.600
Try saying that again!

00:09:14.600 --> 00:09:16.730
You're asking if I know?

00:09:19.020 --> 00:09:21.290
No shit, I know what's gonna happen!

00:09:21.290 --> 00:09:23.610
I'm gonna be just like my mother!

00:09:24.080 --> 00:09:25.610
Your mother?!

00:09:26.220 --> 00:09:29.140
She went insane thanks to drugs!

00:09:29.140 --> 00:09:32.250
My damn mother just let her
body rot till she died!

00:09:32.250 --> 00:09:34.290
I'm gonna be just like that!

00:09:34.730 --> 00:09:39.020
But I'm gonna kill you before I die!

00:09:39.020 --> 00:09:41.250
Then I'll go and kill Il Re while I'm at it!

00:09:43.090 --> 00:09:47.630
With this power, I'll fucking kill
everyone that made me suffer!

00:09:53.960 --> 00:09:58.600
I defeated Lost, the unrivaled Lost.

00:10:05.490 --> 00:10:07.220
What shall I do with you now?

00:10:09.250 --> 00:10:12.350
Should I show you a good time before you die?

00:10:16.350 --> 00:10:17.990
Wouldn't that be fun?

00:10:17.990 --> 00:10:20.170
You're about to die anyway.

00:10:23.980 --> 00:10:27.460
Why don't I just strangle you ever so slowly?

00:10:31.680 --> 00:10:33.480
What a fine glare you have.

00:10:33.480 --> 00:10:35.520
It just makes killing you all
the more worthwhile, really.

00:10:37.560 --> 00:10:40.480
And I still haven't broken any
of the bones in your neck yet.

00:11:03.590 --> 00:11:06.460
F-Fuck!

00:11:07.540 --> 00:11:11.360
What the fuck did you do?!

00:11:46.240 --> 00:11:48.550
Lost...!

00:12:33.020 --> 00:12:33.930
'Sup.

00:12:34.300 --> 00:12:35.110
Yo.

00:12:35.110 --> 00:12:37.370
It's unusual to see you at a place like this.

00:12:38.540 --> 00:12:41.600
You know what happened at the club, right?

00:12:42.480 --> 00:12:43.270
Yeah.

00:12:43.960 --> 00:12:45.850
I heard it was pretty horrific.

00:12:47.200 --> 00:12:51.360
With that place gone, this is
the only joint left to go to.

00:12:53.540 --> 00:12:54.860
Hey Gramps.

00:12:56.580 --> 00:12:59.950
Don't you think things have
been kind of weird lately?

00:13:02.720 --> 00:13:07.460
Toshima might be worthless, but it
used to have a semblance of order.

00:13:10.120 --> 00:13:11.630
You feel it too, don't you?

00:13:14.840 --> 00:13:16.170
I guess.

00:13:16.170 --> 00:13:19.140
Something's different in Toshima now.

00:13:19.140 --> 00:13:20.970
Then you've got some fresh intel?!

00:13:21.670 --> 00:13:23.430
Hold on a minute.

00:13:23.430 --> 00:13:25.190
It's going to cost you.

00:13:25.580 --> 00:13:27.870
Can we exchange information?

00:13:27.870 --> 00:13:29.350
We'll be even then.

00:13:29.660 --> 00:13:31.150
You have some news?

00:13:32.400 --> 00:13:34.840
About the fifty-percent Line.

00:13:36.600 --> 00:13:38.620
Man, you already knew about it?

00:13:38.980 --> 00:13:42.630
Well, for the time being, I
am a pro information broker.

00:13:43.640 --> 00:13:49.710
At any rate, that being marketed out now
means that Vischio are at their limits.

00:13:51.020 --> 00:13:53.380
Thing's suddenly got complicated.

00:13:54.150 --> 00:13:57.380
Yeah. There are also rumours
about an impending civil war.

00:13:57.380 --> 00:14:00.680
Although that rumor isn't really uncommon,

00:14:01.290 --> 00:14:03.350
it does seem like this place has
been caught in the middle of it all.

00:14:04.740 --> 00:14:07.310
This all seemed to happen when
Akira and Keisuke came over, right?

00:14:10.960 --> 00:14:13.230
Something is afoot.

00:14:14.000 --> 00:14:16.700
Civil war and the crumbling of Vischio...

00:14:17.280 --> 00:14:19.870
If it really comes down to those,
it'll be the end of Toshima.

00:14:21.780 --> 00:14:24.080
Then we're out of time.

00:14:26.020 --> 00:14:26.910
Rin!

00:14:27.240 --> 00:14:28.580
Don't overdo it...

00:15:24.720 --> 00:15:25.920
Takky.

00:15:28.150 --> 00:15:29.100
Yukari?

00:15:32.460 --> 00:15:34.470
Dad, Mom!

00:15:34.470 --> 00:15:36.450
Takky's back!

00:15:46.420 --> 00:15:49.870
We'll be together as a
family from now on, right?

00:15:49.870 --> 00:15:50.660
Y-Yeah...

00:15:51.580 --> 00:15:54.920
Soon, I'll defeat Il Re and we'll be rich.

00:15:55.820 --> 00:15:58.310
What are you talking about?

00:15:58.310 --> 00:16:00.340
Didn't you already defeat Il Re?

00:16:00.830 --> 00:16:01.580
Huh—

00:16:10.100 --> 00:16:12.460
Huh, did I?

00:16:12.460 --> 00:16:13.990
Yeah, you did!

00:16:14.410 --> 00:16:18.530
I'm sorry you've had to
experience so many bad things.

00:16:19.860 --> 00:16:23.110
I've been working really
hard for your sake...

00:16:24.550 --> 00:16:29.570
But I never wanted any clothes or toys!

00:16:30.380 --> 00:16:35.100
Just you being here makes me happy!

00:16:37.750 --> 00:16:40.670
I-I'm sorry, Yukari!

00:16:41.810 --> 00:16:42.740
I'm sorry!

00:16:45.890 --> 00:16:47.200
Takky...

00:16:49.280 --> 00:16:50.140
Yukari?!

00:16:51.100 --> 00:16:52.270
Takky!

00:16:52.880 --> 00:16:54.180
Takky!

00:16:55.270 --> 00:16:56.100
Takky!

00:16:56.700 --> 00:16:58.550
Yukari, what's the matter—

00:17:00.900 --> 00:17:02.290
Takky!

00:17:03.220 --> 00:17:04.440
Takky!

00:17:04.440 --> 00:17:05.860
Takky!

00:17:12.380 --> 00:17:15.610
I knew all that from the beginning...

00:17:16.480 --> 00:17:18.250
What the hell have I been doing?

00:17:26.650 --> 00:17:27.810
Yukari!

00:17:50.150 --> 00:17:51.910
Y-You're—

00:17:59.740 --> 00:18:01.780
S-Stop it!

00:18:18.180 --> 00:18:19.360
Yukari!

00:19:42.570 --> 00:19:44.940
Come to think of it, back then...

00:19:53.830 --> 00:19:55.100
...was the same!

00:19:56.010 --> 00:19:58.100
Is my blood—

00:20:04.140 --> 00:20:07.000
Hey, are you looking for someone?

00:20:07.420 --> 00:20:08.500
Keisuke!

00:20:10.450 --> 00:20:11.950
You were all right, then?

00:20:17.520 --> 00:20:20.770
Are you really Keisuke?

00:20:21.380 --> 00:20:23.050
What's with you?

00:20:23.050 --> 00:20:25.140
Forgot what I looked like?

00:20:31.730 --> 00:20:34.610
Keisuke, whose blood is that?

00:20:35.030 --> 00:20:36.470
What, this?

00:20:36.470 --> 00:20:39.370
It's okay; It's not my blood.

00:20:41.520 --> 00:20:46.540
Anyway, I really wanted to see you, Akira.

00:20:49.640 --> 00:20:51.110
What's wrong?

00:20:51.440 --> 00:20:52.760
Don't back away from me.

00:20:53.550 --> 00:20:56.150
Weren't you looking for me?

00:20:57.000 --> 00:20:59.750
Or do you really not care about me?

00:21:00.990 --> 00:21:03.010
That's not the case at all, huh?

00:21:03.010 --> 00:21:04.240
Right, Akira?

00:21:04.240 --> 00:21:05.400
That cross...

00:21:06.080 --> 00:21:07.580
Oh, this?

00:21:08.110 --> 00:21:12.400
Don't worry, I just cleaned a mess up.

00:21:13.230 --> 00:21:17.740
We've finally been reunited. Try
not to focus on the details.

00:21:18.450 --> 00:21:19.520
All right?

00:21:23.300 --> 00:21:26.790
Akira.

00:22:12.560 --> 00:22:15.050
There is no turning back!

00:22:15.930 --> 00:22:17.440
No!

00:22:17.440 --> 00:22:23.250
There is no turning back!

00:22:24.560 --> 00:22:32.650
Nanimo shiranakute Muku na Mama ni Nani wo Motometekitan Darou

00:22:24.560 --> 00:22:32.650
What have I been seeking for, when I
didn't know anything - anything at all?

00:22:34.230 --> 00:22:42.570
Tsunaida Inochii mo Asu no Hikari mo Mou Bokura niwa Nai keredo

00:22:34.230 --> 00:22:42.570
We have neither the future nor the light of tomorrow in our lives anymore,

00:22:42.940 --> 00:22:46.520
Ima Yotteku mono

00:22:42.940 --> 00:22:46.520
but as we kept walking,

00:22:46.870 --> 00:22:53.870
Chiriyuk Yami ni Kizuitanda Negai wa

00:22:46.870 --> 00:22:53.870
we chanced upon the fading darkness

00:22:54.230 --> 00:22:58.890
Hitotsu Dake Mamorenakatta

00:22:54.230 --> 00:22:58.890
There was only one wish we couldn't protect

00:22:59.130 --> 00:23:02.260
Kimi to no Yakusoku to

00:22:59.130 --> 00:23:02.260
in order to keep your promise

00:23:02.560 --> 00:23:05.320
Mirai no Kawari ni

00:23:02.560 --> 00:23:05.320
and protect the future

00:23:06.500 --> 00:23:08.690
I've got to be depressed

00:23:08.900 --> 00:23:16.060
Kawaranai Omoi dake wa Osoi to Shittetemo

00:23:08.900 --> 00:23:16.060
Even if I knew that the
unwavering feelings were mellow...

00:23:16.250 --> 00:23:25.050
Mamorenakatta Kimi to no Yakusoku

00:23:16.250 --> 00:23:25.050
I couldn't keep my promise with you,

00:23:26.020 --> 00:23:33.720
Mamoritakatta Yuitsu no Nukumori

00:23:26.020 --> 00:23:33.720
the one and only warmth I wanted to cherish

00:23:33.720 --> 00:23:35.600
There's no turning back!

00:23:36.640 --> 00:23:38.290
No!

00:23:38.290 --> 00:23:40.470
There is no turning back!

00:23:41.590 --> 00:23:48.040
No!

00:23:50.970 --> 00:23:53.040
Toshima is quite confined, isn't it?

00:23:53.040 --> 00:23:54.050
You think so?

00:23:54.050 --> 00:23:56.350
I keep seeing and meeting
the same people every day.

00:23:56.350 --> 00:23:57.430
What kind of people?

00:23:57.430 --> 00:23:59.670
Like people who suddenly pull out a sword.

00:23:59.670 --> 00:24:02.610
I guess meeting people like
that's pretty common, huh?

00:24:01.490 --> 00:24:04.200
Episode 7
